{"name":"Shark Bait","hex":"#ee6699","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shark bait","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who is in a precarious or vulnerable position.","One who has been, or is likely to be, attacked by a shark.\n\n A lone swimmer or surfer far from shore."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shark_bait"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shark cage diving","blocks":[{"text":"Shark cage diving is underwater diving or snorkeling where the observer remains inside a protective cage designed to prevent sharks from making contact with the divers. Shark cage diving is used for scientific observation, underwater cinematography, and as a tourist activity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Sharks_outside_cage.jpg/330px-Sharks_outside_cage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shark_cage_diving"},{"title":"Shark Bait (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Shark Bait is a 2006 animated adventure film."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6a/Shark_Bait_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shark_Bait_(film)"},{"title":"Shark","blocks":[{"text":"Sharks are a group of elasmobranch cartilaginous fishes characterized by a ribless endoskeleton, dermal denticles, five to seven gill slits on each side, and pectoral fins that are not fused to the head. Modern sharks are classified within the division Selachii and are the sister group to the Batomorphi. Some sources extend the term \"shark\" as an informal category including extinct members of Chondrichthyes with a shark-like morphology, such as hybodonts. Shark-like chondrichthyans such as Cladoselache and Doliodus first appeared in the Devonian Period, though some fossilized chondrichthyan-like scales are as old as the Late Ordovician. The earliest confirmed modern sharks (Selachii) are known from the Early Jurassic around 200 million years ago, with the oldest known member being Agaleus, though records of true sharks may extend back as far as the Permian."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Corl0207_%2828225976491%29.jpg/330px-Corl0207_%2828225976491%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shark"},{"title":"Bait","blocks":[{"text":"Bait is any appetizing substance used to attract prey when hunting or fishing, most commonly in the form of trapping, ambushing and angling."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Tapette.jpg/330px-Tapette.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bait"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Great_white_shark_cages_at_Isla_Guadalupe%2C_Mexico%2C_November_2017._Shark_cage_diving_with_the_MV_Horizon._Animal_estimated_at_16-18_feet_in_length%2C_age_unknown.png/500px-thumbnail.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Great_white_shark_cages_at_Isla_Guadalupe%2C_Mexico%2C_November_2017._Shark_cage_diving_with_the_MV_Horizon._Animal_estimated_at_16-18_feet_in_length%2C_age_unknown.png/1280px-thumbnail.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Great_white_shark_cages_at_Isla_Guadalupe%2C_Mexico%2C_November_2017._Shark_cage_diving_with_the_MV_Horizon._Animal_estimated_at_16-18_feet_in_length%2C_age_unknown.png/500px-thumbnail.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Great white shark cages at Isla Guadalupe, Mexico","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGreat_white_shark_cages_at_Isla_Guadalupe%2C_Mexico%2C_November_2017._Shark_cage_diving_wi